{
  "_README": [
    "TEMPLATE 2 of 4 — INDUSTRIES SERVED OVERVIEW  (/industries-served)",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS FIXES vs your live markup",
    "  1. Your list items are typed WebPage; the services overview types its items Service.",
    "     Two hub pages, two different models. Industry pages describe a SERVICE delivered to a",
    "     specific audience, so Service is the correct type on both — with audience narrowing it.",
    "  2. Item 8 is labelled 'Telecom & Aerospace' but points at",
    "     /industries-served/test-measurement-equipment. Label and destination disagree. Pick one.",
    "  3. No business entity on the page, so no local signals.",
    "  4. No image declared. The page has a hero at industry-overview-hero.png that nothing",
    "     references, and og:image points at the logo.",
    "  5. Item entries carry no description or image.",
    "",
    "THE KEY IDEA — this is what makes the industry pages pull their weight:",
    "Each entry declares BOTH the audience it serves AND the compliance regime that audience",
    "carries. That is the structured-data expression of 'we do healthcare recycling with HIPAA",
    "and HITECH focus that we would not apply elsewhere'. Google reads audience + about, and",
    "the differentiation becomes machine-readable instead of only being prose.",
    "",
    "RICH RESULT ELIGIBILITY: Breadcrumbs.",
    "Strip all _README and _comment keys before shipping."
  ],

